  "_readme": "SAMPLE / DEMO DATA ONLY. Northern Ireland postcode-to-coordinate data (unit level) is published by Land & Property Services (LPS) as the 'Pointer' dataset via the NI Open Data portal (opendatani.gov.uk) under the NI Open Government Licence. It is not bundled with ONSPD/Code-Point Open in the same way GB data is, which is why it needs handling separately (see README). This file covers all ~80 real NI postcode districts (outward codes) with an approximate centroid each — mostly the district's post town (geocoded via OpenStreetMap Nominatim), except Belfast's own sub-districts (BT1/2/7/9/12/15) which have distinct, more specific coordinates. This is still DISTRICT-level, not unit-level — replace src/postcode.js's NI provider with a loader for the real Pointer CSV for production/unit-level accuracy.",
